diff --git a/docs/config.md b/docs/config.md
index 7615f82..6b85bdb 100644
--- a/docs/config.md
+++ b/docs/config.md
@@ -446,0 +447,21 @@ Try `True` when the calling pipeline supports PDL and adjacent kernels have work
+
+### Grouped-mask input processing with changing batches
+
+With `layout="grouped_mask"` and `zero_invalid=False`, input processing uses
+fixed workers per expert and reads the valid row counts from the device on each
+invocation. The workers iterate over valid rows while preserving the padded
+input/output addresses and scale layout. A captured CUDA Graph can therefore
+handle changing expert counts, including empty experts and later recovery,
+without reading counts back to the CPU or rebuilding the graph.
+
+This changes work scheduling, not allocation capacity. The caller must still
+reserve enough rows for the largest supported batch and routing skew. Counts
+must describe rows within each expert's allocated capacity. Input row count is
+the MoE batch size, not the attention context length.
+
+When PDL is enabled, workers wait for producer dependencies before reading
+counts and signal dependents only after all assigned rows are processed. Even
+empty workers participate in dependency completion. `zero_invalid=True` keeps
+the padded-row launch so invalid output rows and scales retain their documented
+zeroing behavior. The separate group/token scale finalizer also keeps its
+existing launch layout.
